   "id": "root",
   "x": 457,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Sodium is off: is water LOST (Na > 144) or RETAINED (Na < 136)?",
   "lines": [
    "both are almost always WATER problems, not sodium problems",
    "find the CAUSE, and correct only as fast as the brain can adapt (CORRECT row)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_hyper",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 138,
   "w": 660,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "HYPERnatremia (Na > 144): free water LOST · cells SHRINK",
   "lines": [
    "unusual unless THIRST, ACCESS to water or ability to DRINK fails",
    "1 · extracellular fluid (ECF) volume HIGH → sodium GAIN: sea water, IV fluids, mineralocorticoid excess"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_hypo",
   "x": 745,
   "y": 138,
   "w": 884,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "HYPOnatremia (Na < 136): water RETAINED · cells SWELL",
   "lines": [
    "1 · plasma osmolality (Osm) HIGH or normal → PSEUDOhyponatremia: glucose, mannitol (Na falls 1 per 3–4 rise in glucose)"
   ]
  },
  {
